Module origin "The salt-pans" {
  Kind chapter. Entity title: chapter "The salt-pans".
  Entity party: group "You".
  Place shop "The salt-house" is room.
  Entity salter: group "The salter". Entity cold: fact "The pans are going cold". Entity work: fact "Work at the pans".
  Relation wagePaid(group).
  // A week's wage owed both ways: the salter owes it, and cannot pay it until the salt is sold.
  Entity wage: fact "{merchant} owes you a week's wage, eighteen coin. It cannot be paid until the season's salt is sold.".
  Initially Assert established(wage). Initially Assert knows(party, cold). Initially Assert knows(party, wage).
  Observe arrival at shop as fixture when watch(clock) < 1 "Grey light through the salt-house door at {town}, and your breath smoking. All night you fed the last hearth with barrel-staves and broken crates. It was not enough. By dawn two of the three pans had a skin of salt on them like ice on a pond.".
  Observe charge at shop as feature when watch(clock) < 2 "{merchant} stands at the door looking up the river toward {fuelvillage}, as {merchant} has every hour since the day before yesterday. 'Two days late,' {merchant} says, without turning. 'Three days cold and the brine goes off. Then the season is lost, and your wage with it.' Then, turning: 'I can't leave the pans. You can.'".
  Topic wage with salter "Ask {merchant} for your week's wage" when knows(actor, work) and not wagePaid(actor) once {
    Says "{merchant} looks at the steam going up off the pans. Then {merchant} goes to the strongbox. Eighteen coin, counted out twice. 'A week, and a boat,' {merchant} says. 'I'd not have had either without you.'".
    On discuss { Increase quantity(actor, gold) by 18. Assert wagePaid(actor). }
  }
  Goal false.
}
